{
  "comment": [
    "One row for each decision of `decide` and of the scope rule of the calls_heap producer",
    "(src/fort/ownership_source_calls.ft): the gaps of a call, the summaries that a caller can",
    "apply, the budget errors that exclude a body, the candidates that keep it declared, the",
    "solver status and the proof, and the unexecuted rows of a closure without a graph proof",
    "(src/fort/ownership_source.ft). The rows named report-calls-* and calls-* hold the records,",
    "the budget errors and the ledgers that the report gives for the producer",
    "(src/fort/ownership_report.ft). A row names the line that holds the rule and the text that",
    "breaks it. The build compiles working-tree HEAD with the mutant, and the module tests compile",
    "src/fort with the mutant too. The stages run the producer and report tests, then the",
    "ownership driver test. Run it in the Linux VM with the release preset, after the same stages",
    "pass on the unmutated tree."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "src/fort/ownership_report.ft",
    "src/fort/ownership_source.ft",
    "src/fort/ownership_source_calls.ft"
  ],
  "binary": "build/Linux/release/fort",
  "build": "ninja -C build/Linux/release fort fort_std",
  "stages": [
    {
      "name": "calls producer tests",
      "command": "python3 test/lang/run_tests.py --root test/fort --fort build/Linux/release/fort --std-dir build/Linux/release/std --timeout 900 -j 6 ownership_source_calls ownership_report_calls"
    },
    {
      "name": "ownership driver",
      "command": "python3 test/ownership_driver_test.py --fort build/Linux/release/fort --std-dir build/Linux/release/std --cc /usr/bin/clang --opt /usr/bin/opt-18"
    }
  ],
